# Settings for the local run (run-local.ps1 / Ctrl+Shift+B in VS Code).
# Copy this file to .env.local (git ignores it) and fill in the lines marked  <-- ADD.
# Everything else (ports, dev keys for LiveKit, Temporal and the orchestrator) is preset.
#
# The assistant needs speech credentials for BOTH voice and chat sessions: it speaks
# every answer, and the chat text is published as the speech is played.
# Fill in ONE of the two options below. If both are set, Azure is used.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- option 1: Azure AI Speech (recommended)
# Same service as the Azure test environment. Find the values in the Azure portal:
#   resource group of your test environment (rg-<prefix>) > speech-<prefix>-... resource
#   > Resource Management > Keys and Endpoint: "KEY 1" and "Location/Region".
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=                      # <-- ADD: your KEY 1 (32 characters)
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=switzerlandnorth   # change only if your Speech resource is in another region

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- option 2: Deepgram + Cartesia
# Used only when AZURE_SPEECH_KEY is empty. Needs both keys.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=                      # <-- ADD (option 2 only): speech-to-text key from console.deepgram.com
CARTESIA_API_KEY=                      # <-- ADD (option 2 only): text-to-speech key from play.cartesia.ai
